## 3. Scientific Research Restriction

Without prior written permission from the relevant copyright holder(s), you may **NOT** use NetworkTools, substantial portions of its source code, or a substantially derived implementation as part of another:

- student scientific research project;
- scientific research submission;
- university research project;
- research competition;
- innovation competition;
- technology competition;
- graduation thesis;
- capstone project;
- academic project requiring original implementation;
- academic publication;
- research prototype submitted for assessment;
- software project presented as independently developed work.

This restriction applies whether NetworkTools is:

- copied directly;
- partially copied;
- translated to another programming language;
- reorganized into another architecture;
- modified;
- renamed;
- visually redesigned;
- combined with other software;
- or otherwise adapted.

NetworkTools may still be used as a **reference or comparison project**, provided that proper attribution is given and its source code is not incorporated into the submitted work in violation of this License.

